WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.640
A whole-body knockout can kill the embryo, and it cannot say which tissue needed the

2
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:16.520
gene. So you want a gene gone only in chosen cells, and maybe only at a chosen time.

3
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.600
In 1994, Gu and colleagues deleted a piece of DNA polymerase beta in T cells only.

4
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.300
The mice were viable, although the matching germline mutation is lethal.

5
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:33.683
Cre is an enzyme from a bacterial virus.

6
00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:38.903
It cuts DNA at a 34-base-pair site called loxP.

7
00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:43.763
A floxed gene has a piece flanked by two loxP sites.

8
00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:46.743
It works normally until Cre acts.

9
00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:52.203
When two sites point the same way, Cre cuts out the DNA between them.

10
00:00:53.517 --> 00:01:00.417
Cross a floxed mouse to a mouse that makes Cre from a promoter active in one cell

11
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:03.757
type. Only those cells lose the gene.

12
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:06.297
This is a conditional knockout.

13
00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:12.697
A second design puts a stop between loxP sites in front of a reporter gene.

14
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:18.497
Cre cuts the stop out, and the reporter is read in that cell and all its

15
00:01:18.497 --> 00:01:22.457
descendants. A glowing cell shows that Cre acted.

16
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.910
For timing, fuse Cre to a modified estrogen receptor.

17
00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.010
It stays out of the nucleus until tamoxifen is given.

18
00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:39.450
Flp, from yeast, cuts at its own FRT sites and does not recognize loxP.

19
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:47.250
In flies, a yeast activator called GAL4, made in chosen cells, switches on a target

20
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.390
gene with GAL4 binding sites.

21
00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:54.223
A real result: Luo and colleagues, 2020.

22
00:01:55.423 --> 00:01:59.363
Floxed Clstn3 mice were crossed with a Cre line.

23
00:02:00.363 --> 00:02:03.743
Offspring should inherit only intact floxed alleles.

24
00:02:04.643 --> 00:02:10.003
When the mother carried Cre, 73 of 83 offspring had a knockout allele.

25
00:02:10.923 --> 00:02:14.763
When the father carried Cre, none of 114 did.

26
00:02:15.703 --> 00:02:18.043
Look only at offspring without Cre.

27
00:02:18.773 --> 00:02:23.263
From Cre mothers, 29 of 34 had one deleted copy.

28
00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:29.183
A deleted allele in an animal with no Cre cannot be Cre acting in that animal.

29
00:02:29.783 --> 00:02:31.163
It points to the germline.

30
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:35.277
First, a reporter is not a deletion.

31
00:02:35.997 --> 00:02:38.557
A glowing cell may still carry the gene.

32
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:45.217
The control: measure the target protein or DNA in reporter-positive cells in the

33
00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:52.457
same animals. Second, germline recombination was reported in over half of 64

34
00:02:52.457 --> 00:02:55.257
commonly used nervous-system Cre lines.

35
00:02:55.257 --> 00:02:59.857
Genotype every animal, and check animals without Cre.

36
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:09.900
In 2007, Guy, Bird and colleagues silenced the gene Mecp2 with a removable

37
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.320
lox-stop cassette, then restored it with tamoxifen-activated Cre.

38
00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.240
Advanced symptoms reversed in young and mature adult mice.

39
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:27.480
In 2012, Fünfschilling, Nave and colleagues deleted Cox10 in oligodendrocytes and

40
00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:33.980
Schwann cells. Conditional deletion was needed to remove respiration only in glial cells.

41
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:43.020
In 2016, Orefice, Ginty and colleagues deleted Mecp2 in peripheral somatosensory

42
00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.660
neurons and caused tactile dysfunction.

43
00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:53.280
Restoring Mecp2 only in these neurons rescued tactile sensitivity, but not

44
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.880
lethality. Keep this rule.

45
00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.700
A reporter shows where Cre acted, not that your gene is gone.
